  "worked_solution": "First, we find the orthogonal projection matrix onto ${S}^{\u22a5}=\\text{Span}{a}.$\n\nUsing the formula for the orthogonal projection matrix\n\n$$\n{P}_{{S}^{\u22a5}}=a({a}^{T}\\,a)^{-1}{a}^{T},\n$$\n\nwe obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{{S}^{\u22a5}} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]{([\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={18}^{-1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 4 & 16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that ${P}_{S}+{P}_{{S}^{\u22a5}}=I.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{S} & =I-{P}_{{S}^{\u22a5}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{18}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 4 & 16\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}[\\begin{aligned}17 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 17 & -4 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${p}_{23}+{p}_{31}=(-4)+4=0.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
